        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Liu Wei often works at night. He searches in parking lots. He hides himself in dense grass. He carefully checks underground "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pipelines",
            "zh": "管道"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The 35-year-old man from Shanghai is a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "detective",
            "ref": "v-detective"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". He’s not catching criminals, though. Instead, he’s looking for people’s missing pets."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Since 2012, Liu has helped to find more than 1,000 cats, dogs and even "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "lizards",
            "ref": "v-lizard"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for their owners. In his experience, cats have a better chance of being discovered. “They just hide,” he said. “They wouldn’t go far.” Dogs, however, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "are more likely to",
            "ref": "v-be-more-likely-to"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " be stolen. This makes finding a missing dog more difficult."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The pet detective business has been growing fast in recent years as more people keep pets at home. "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Hiring",
            "ref": "v-hire"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a pet detective is not cheap. It can cost more than 10,000 yuan, but it’s worth it for pet owners. “They’re not animals,” Liu said. “They’re members of the family.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
